+<intent-contract>
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** CI logs are noisy — the full frai-gate report takes multiple lines and is hard to parse at a glance. Users need a compact one-line summary for CI logs to quickly see the gate verdict and which checks have issues.
+
+**Approach:** Add `renderSummary(result: GateResult): string` function to render gate results as `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>[:checkIds]`, then wire it to a new `--summary` flag on `frai-gate check` that prints only the summary line instead of the full report.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Format is exactly `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>` where total = 7 (GATE_CHECKS.length) and answered = checks with no block-severity findings
+- Warnings do not reduce answered count
+- When block findings exist for GATE_CHECKS, append `: ` and their check ids comma-and-space separated, in GATE_CHECKS order, each id once (e.g., `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency`)
+- Structure finding (missing gate section) returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` (answered is 0 because no checks could be evaluated)
+- Exit codes remain: 1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise
+- `--json` flag takes priority if both `--summary` and `--json` are provided
+
+**Never:**
+- Do not modify existing renderText/renderJson behavior
+- Do not change CLI exit codes
+- Do not add renderSummary to default output (only via flag)
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|-----------------|----------------|
+| All checks pass | GateResult with verdict=PASS, 0 findings | `PASS 7/7` | No error |
+| Warnings only | GateResult with verdict=WARN, findings w/ severity=warn | `WARN 7/7` (no IDs, since no blocks reduce answered) | No error |
+| Block findings | GateResult with verdict=BLOCK, block findings in evaluation, transparency | `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency` | No error |
+| Missing gate section | GateResult with gateSection=null | `BLOCK 0/7: structure` | No error |
+| Multiple block checks | GateResult with blocks in risk-tier, evaluation, monitoring | `BLOCK 4/7: risk-tier, evaluation, monitoring` | No error |
+| --summary with --json | CLI receives both flags | Renders JSON (--json takes priority) | No error |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
