+- `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/report.test.ts` -- Create test file with cases for renderSummary -- Covers all edge cases: PASS/WARN/BLOCK, missing section, multiple block checks
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given a gate result with verdict PASS and no findings, when renderSummary is called, then output is "PASS 7/7"
+- Given a gate result with verdict WARN and one warning finding (severity=warn) in evaluation, when renderSummary is called, then output is "WARN 7/7" (warnings do not reduce answered count, no IDs listed)
+- Given a gate result with verdict WARN and warning findings in evaluation and monitoring, when renderSummary is called, then output is "WARN 7/7" (multiple warnings still don't reduce answered)
+- Given a gate result with verdict BLOCK and block findings (severity=block) in evaluation and transparency (in that GATE_CHECKS order), when renderSummary is called, then output is "BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency"
+- Given a gate result with verdict BLOCK and block in evaluation and warning in monitoring, when renderSummary is called, then output is "BLOCK 6/7: evaluation" (only blocks listed, blocks reduce answered)
+- Given a gate result with gateSection null (structure finding), when renderSummary is called, then output is "BLOCK 0/7: structure"
+- Given CLI args with both --summary and --json, when cmdCheck runs, then --json takes priority and outputs JSON, not summary
+- Given CLI args with --summary flag, when cmdCheck runs, then only the summary line is printed and exit code is correct (1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise)
